<template>
    <heading>Operations</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>operations</li>
        <li>generator</li>
        <li>coroutine</li>
        <li>command handler</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>to_handler</li>
        <li>modal dialog</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code><![CDATA[operations]]></code> holds the application's multi-step command handlers. Each handler is a generator object, created and primed by <code><![CDATA[to_handler]]></code>. The generator receives <code><![CDATA[self]]></code>, a function that returns its own object; calling <code><![CDATA[self()]]></code> after construction avoids accessing the object before it exists.</p>
        <p>Each operation can produce one of three outcomes when <code><![CDATA[controller]]></code> resumes it with <code><![CDATA[handler.next(command)]]></code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><code><![CDATA[yield self()]]></code>: remain the current handler. The controller stops dispatching this command; the next command resumes the same operation.</li>
            <li><code><![CDATA[yield child]]></code>, where <code><![CDATA[child]]></code> is another primed generator object: call a child operation. The controller pushes <code><![CDATA[child]]></code> onto <code><![CDATA[handlerStack]]></code> and immediately dispatches the same command to it.</li>
            <li><code><![CDATA[return]]></code>, or reach the end of the generator: finish the operation. The generator result has <code><![CDATA[done === true]]></code>, so the controller pops it and resumes the parent with the same command. Any returned value is ignored. If no parent remains, dispatch ends.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>A <code><![CDATA[ModalDialog]]></code> command carries a <code><![CDATA[dialogName]]></code> key identifying the dialog-specific operation. The base handler switches on that key and yields the selected primed operation. The controller then sends the same initial command to the child.</p>
        <p><code><![CDATA[SelectCreateProject]]></code> is the operation for the startup project dialog. It receives the initial command and calls <code><![CDATA[showModalDialog]]></code> with the dialog template's DOM id. The helper finds that child template inside <code><![CDATA[LP5-Dialog-Templates]]></code>, clones its content, prepends a clone of the first child shared modal style, appends the content to the document body, and calls <code><![CDATA[showModal()]]></code>. It returns immediately; the operation remains the active handler and can receive later commands while the dialog is open.</p>
        <p><code><![CDATA[operations]]></code> installs the primed base handler with <code><![CDATA[controller.init(handler)]]></code> before any commands are dispatched.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Outermost scope objects</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
let operations = (() => {
    function to_handler(generator) {
        const handler = generator(() => handler);
        handler.next();
        return handler;
    }

    function showModalDialog(dialogName) {
        const templates = document.getElementById("LP5-Dialog-Templates");
        if (!(templates instanceof HTMLTemplateElement))
            throw new Error("Missing LP5-Dialog-Templates template");

        const template = templates.content.querySelector(`#${dialogName}`);
        if (!(template instanceof HTMLTemplateElement))
            throw new Error(`Missing dialog template: ${dialogName}`);

        const sharedStyle = templates.content.firstElementChild;
        if (!(sharedStyle instanceof HTMLStyleElement))
            throw new Error("Missing shared dialog styles");

        const content = template.content.cloneNode(true);
        content.prepend(sharedStyle.cloneNode(true));

        const dialog = content.querySelector("dialog");
        if (!dialog)
            throw new Error(`Dialog template has no dialog element: ${dialogName}`);

        document.body.append(content);
        dialog.showModal();
    }

    function* SelectCreateProject(self) {
        let command = yield self();
        showModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");
        while (true) {
            command = yield self();
        }
    }

    function* baseOperationsHandler(self) {
        while (true) {
            let command = yield self();
            if (command.name === "ModalDialog") {
                switch (command.dialogName) {
                case "SelectCreateProject":
                    yield to_handler(SelectCreateProject);
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    const handler = to_handler(baseOperationsHandler);
    controller.init(handler);

    return {};
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
